## Context

The deterministic half of consolidation: pool the tiers, group candidates,
report, and instrument. The judged half — deciding whether a group is one
lesson and writing the merged text — is `0916`, and keeping the two apart is
what lets this half be tested.

Promotion currently identifies entries by filename equality, which yields one
candidate. A lexical pass finds roughly 43 candidate pairs of which 17–21 are
genuine, so the mechanism is not short of material; it is short of a way to
recognise it.

Design reference: defect 2 and "What the consolidation pass does" in `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md`.

## Relevant files

- `skills/dream/SKILL.md` — the pass
- `skills/dream/provenance.py` — candidacy and the walker

## Actions

1. Pool the project directories **and the harness tier**, which participates on
   the same footing. The one asymmetry is a direction: promotion moves up into
   the harness tier and never back out, so a pair straddling the two resolves in
   advance — harness copy survives, project copy is tombstoned.
2. Group candidates mechanically and hand the groups to `0916`.
3. Report near-miss pairs — similar enough to suspect, different enough not to
   merge — as contradiction candidates.
4. Keep a **rejection ledger**: a pair a human rejected once must not be
   re-proposed every run.
5. Record body count and the pass's wall-clock duration, **with a threshold
   that fails a test**. A duration written to a log is not an alarm; an alarm
   has a threshold and a reader.
6. Refuse to run against a checkout with uncommitted bodies, and hold a run
   lock so two passes cannot interleave. An overwritten uncommitted body has no
   ancestor to recover from.

## Test

Red first, and these fixtures are reused by `0916`: a known-genuine pair is
surfaced; the named lexical false positive (`dropna_before_merge` /
`rebase_before_merge`) is not; a pair straddling project and harness tiers is
grouped with the resolution direction recorded. Plus: a dirty checkout is
refused; a second pass blocks on the lock; a duration over threshold fails.

## Verification

- [ ] Candidates rise from 1 to the genuine pairs, false positives excluded
- [ ] A rejected pair is not re-proposed on the next run
- [ ] The lock and the dirty-tree refusal both fire in tests

## Invariants

- This ticket merges nothing. It proposes.
- Nothing is deleted.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The three grouping fixtures pass
- [ ] Rejection ledger persists across runs, proven by a fixture
- [ ] Duration threshold fails a test when exceeded
- [ ] Dirty-tree refusal and run lock each proven by a fixture
